WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.800
Exposure management starts with an inventory of important accounts, profiles, domains,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.790
repositories, public documents, services, and third-party references.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.781
Review them as an external visitor would,

00:00:10.781 --> 00:00:16.763
then compare what is visible with what the person or organization intends to disclose.

00:00:16.763 --> 00:00:21.462
Individuals can tighten privacy settings, remove unnecessary contact or location details,

00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:24.026
close unused accounts, review old posts,

00:00:24.026 --> 00:00:27.017
and keep professional profiles accurate and consistent.

00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:32.144
Strong unique passwords and multi-factor authentication reduce the chance that an existing

00:00:32.144 --> 00:00:34.280
footprint becomes an account compromise.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.843
Review photographs and documents before publication.

00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:41.543
Remove unnecessary metadata where appropriate, check visible backgrounds and embedded comments,

00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:43.679
and use approved organizational templates.

00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:46.243
Avoid sharing schedules, credentials, private addresses,

00:00:46.243 --> 00:00:47.952
or security-sensitive operational details.

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:52.224
Organizations need recurring review processes rather than one cleanup event.

00:00:52.224 --> 00:00:56.924
Assign owners for public assets, domains, repositories, documents, and social accounts.

00:00:56.924 --> 00:01:01.624
Integrate exposure checks into publishing, employee onboarding and departure, project closure,

00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:03.333
procurement, and incident response.

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:08.460
Employee awareness should explain why ordinary public details can combine into risk

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.596
without encouraging fear or secrecy.

00:01:10.596 --> 00:01:14.869
Provide clear reporting channels for suspected exposure and respond constructively.

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:18.714
Monitoring should focus on organizational assets and authorized purposes,

00:01:18.714 --> 00:01:20.850
not covert surveillance of staff.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.986
Track remediation and verify results.

00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:25.977
Some third-party copies or indexes may persist,

00:01:25.977 --> 00:01:29.822
so record residual risk and follow appropriate removal processes.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:34.949
The goal is a deliberate footprint that supports legitimate communication and operations

00:01:34.949 --> 00:01:37.940
while reducing avoidable privacy and security exposure.
